---
# Focused on the failure modes that actually matter in a latency-sensitive
# engine: lifetime bugs, silent narrowing, accidental copies, and undefined
# behaviour. Stylistic checks are deliberately excluded -- clang-format owns
# formatting, and a wall of naming warnings trains people to ignore the tool.
#
# Why each check below is disabled. These notes live here, above the list,
# rather than inside it: `Checks:` is a YAML folded scalar, so every indented
# line is part of the string and a '#' there is text rather than a comment.
# Writing the rationale inline silently swallowed four of the exclusions into a
# garbage check name, and the enforcing CI job is what found that.
#
#   modernize-use-nodiscard
#       Fires on every const accessor in the project, 818 of them, which is
#       how a useful idea becomes noise. [[nodiscard]] belongs by hand on the
#       command-path results, where discarding one means discarding a
#       rejection.
#
#   modernize-avoid-c-arrays
#       Flags std::unique_ptr<std::byte[]> in the pool allocator, a
#       runtime-sized buffer with no std::array equivalent. The fixed-size
#       arrays this check was right about are now std::array.
#
#   modernize-use-transparent-functors
#       std::map<Price, PriceLevel, std::greater<Price>> names its
#       comparator's type on purpose. The transparent form buys heterogeneous
#       lookup, which nothing here does, and hides what is being compared.
#
#   misc-no-recursion
#       FlatHashMap::insert and grow call each other, bounded at depth two:
#       grow rehashes into a table sized for the elements it already holds, so
#       the inner insert cannot grow again. Restructuring a hot path to
#       satisfy a lint is the wrong trade.
#
#   cert-dcl58-cpp
#       Specialising std::hash for a program-defined type is explicitly
#       permitted by [namespace.std], which is exactly what include/xc/core/
#       ids.hpp does. The check cannot tell that apart from genuinely adding
#       declarations to namespace std.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  cert-*,
  -cert-err58-cpp,
  -cert-dcl58-cpp,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-member-init,
  cppcoreguidelines-slicing,
  misc-*,
  -misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -misc-no-recursion,
  modernize-*,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -modernize-use-nodiscard,
  -modernize-avoid-c-arrays,
  -modernize-use-transparent-functors,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-braces-around-statements,
  readability-const-return-type,
  readability-misleading-indentation,
  readability-redundant-*
# Everything surviving the exclusions above is worth acting on, so CI treats
# them as errors. A lint that only warns is a lint that accumulates: this
# configuration sat in the repository unenforced until it had 1229 outstanding
# findings, one of which was a real durability bug.
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*/(include|src|apps|bench|fuzz)/.*'
FormatStyle: file
